// ── Hardware Prelude — CIRCT / Cell Targets ──────────────────────────────
// 2026-07-21: Rewritten with direct AST navigation DSL.
// 2026-07-23: Added Count$ check — Before$ on empty selection causes error.
// Used by .sbv files.
//
// 2026-09-25 (E9, plan `2026-09-21-hardware-dialect-gaps.md`): the import
// insert is DROPPED. It injected `std/hardware.bv`, a file that never
// existed in `lib/std/` — so every `.sbv` program with at least one user
// import failed with "Cannot find module 'std/hardware.bv'". The silicon
// dialect needs no stdlib content today: sized scalars (`UInt<8>`),
// registers (`reg let`), and every operator are compiler intrinsics, and
// `.sbv` bans frgn/link anyway. The slot stays in the prelude family so
// `--no-std` and the per-extension config keep one name for `.sbv`.
//
// When a real silicon stdlib lands (a `lib/std/hardware.bv` with content
// a hardware program actually needs), re-add the insert here:
//
//     let anchor = Tag$("import").First$();
//     when anchor.Count$() > 0 {
//         anchor.Before$().Insert$(Import$("std/hardware.bv"));
//     };
//
// Rule: never re-add the import before the file exists — no placeholder
// module, no empty file (Rule 7 / ALWAYS FINISH applies to it).

